                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers [/h1]\n\nSo I bought & played 13 minutes of this hellish game in tribute to the series 13 Reasons Why. You will be asking yourself, \"Why?\", if you do indeed decide to make the same mistake I did. This game has nothing to offer. Just like death itself. It is the end and the means. \n\nIs there any game fun to be had here? No. Does this game offer anything interesting? No. Does it run smoothly? No. Is it bug free? No. Is .99 cents too much asking price for this game? Yes. Well, what exactly is this game?\n\nWell, it's a school-building. It actually looks nice. So once you've gone around the building you've basically done everything. Well, what about jumping from the building you ask?\n\nYes, you can touch a butterfly and rocket up to the top of the building and then jump off. I would imagine this dev dreams of doing that (I mean look at his other game, OldMaidGirl - which is a pedo game disguised as a card game and I would imagine anyone who likes fondling a little girl in VR probably does want to kill themselves).  But there's nothing fun or interesting about it. \n\nThe fall doesn't even feel right. It's like taking a quick elevator down. Then you see some red splatter on your screen. The thing is laughably bad. There's other VR games that let you feel that sense of falling much better, if you want a cool version try Ultimate Booster Experience, where one of the rides is bungee jumping off a skyscraper and that fall is way more exciting and fun and less ghastly.\n\nThe game also had several graphical errors and I got stuck in a stairwell and had to restart. It also has several pop-in issues. I had to quit and restart 3 times because of various issues.\n\nRate 3/10. Do NOT buy. I paid .99 cents so you don't have to.",
